WEBVTT

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.380
Once we made up our mind, we rushed headlong.

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:09.100
We gave up on Earth as a lost cause, once and for all,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.070
and we tried to believe in Jovian righteousness.

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:14.920
But their righteousness wasn't righteousness for us.

00:00:15.590 --> 00:00:17.820
Passion, friendship, industriousness...

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.170
There were as many right ways as there were people.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:57.530
12 Hours after Tsukumo's assassination

00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:12.610
Now, the Commander of the Jovian Federation Yuujin Forces,

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.600
Lieutenant General Kusakabe Haruki,

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:18.200
will give his commemoration speech for the special promotion of Colonel Shiratori Tsukumo.

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:29.070
Our mission is to bring about peace in space and build  a prosperous future for all of humanity.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:34.490
"Being Myself", Being Yourself

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:35.800
The realization of our enduring dreams.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.400
"Being Myself", Being Yourself

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:37.510
Jovian Federation Mother Ship Reigetsu

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.290
We do not seek war.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:39.700
Jovian Federation Mother Ship Reigetsu

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.300
Losing lives for no real reason is truly meaningless.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:42.550
Jovian Federation Mother Ship Reigetsu

00:02:43.150 --> 00:02:45.890
But our proposal was answered by the United Earth Government

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.740
with the cowardly murder of our Ambassador Plenipotentiary,

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:51.520
Colonel Shiratori Tsukumo!

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:54.150
You must not lose hope!

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:55.730
There is only one true righteousness!

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:03.200
No doubt, we will defeat the evil Earth!

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.870
So watch closely, my dear friends!

00:03:06.390 --> 00:03:10.480
Just as in episode 39 of
"Hot Blooded Robot, Gekiganger 3,"

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:14.040
we will fight. Righteousness always prevails!

00:03:15.110 --> 00:03:18.720
Everyone, it's time to roar our slogan for justice!

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:19.920
Let's...

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.880
GEKIGA-IN!

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:30.180
Hey, you jerks!

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:32.540
We were invited on board, you know!

00:03:32.990 --> 00:03:34.710
Hey, you! Can't you answer someone?

00:03:34.710 --> 00:03:35.620
Don't let it bother you.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:36.480
Erina-san...

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.230
We don't have much time. Please forgive us.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:40.370
Time?

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:42.280
Why don't we start now?

00:03:42.810 --> 00:03:44.160
Akito, Captain...

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:49.200
I'll explain later. First I want you to think about Mars.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.950
Kakitsubata has created a boson jump field.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.880
Is the ship itself going to boson jump?!

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.930
Boson readings increasing.

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:05.370
No! There are hundreds of people on board!

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:09.700
Hello! Come in, Kakitsubata! Kakitsubata?!

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.900
What? What's going on?

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.380
Both of you, think back.

00:04:15.630 --> 00:04:16.340
Inez-san?

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.520
Think back, Akito-kun, Captain, about Mars.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.240
About all the wonderful days at the Utopia Colony.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:26.740
Akito!

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:29.470
What's happening to me?

00:04:30.420 --> 00:04:31.080
Yurika!

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:36.240
Kakitsubata is beginning its boson jump.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.440
Akatsuki-san, please respond!

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.440
Akatsuki-san! Akatsuki-san!

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.630
Damn it, Akatsuki, answer me!

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:49.050
Tenkawa Akito and two others remain unaccounted for.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:50.780
Continue with all monitoring, please!

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:52.060
This is going to be a momentous occasion.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:54.490
I'm counting on you, Tenkawa-kun.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:56.810
They're back!

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.110
What?!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.800
This looks like the observation dome of the Kakitsubata.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:04.860
I guess even in space,

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.950
people instinctively choose to be at a place from which they can see all the surrounding scenery.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:14.080
Remember the time we boson jumped from Mars to the Moon.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:15.960
We also found ourselves in the observation room.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.150
That time?

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:23.990
That was so unfair. They all treated us like slackers.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:25.220
But why was that?

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.260
We will find that out now.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.120
Now, concentrate and visualize.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:36.560
Mars, Utopia Colony...

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.070
Mars... Mars...

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:01.760
Tenkawa-kun!

00:06:01.760 --> 00:06:02.470
Can we make it?

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:10.260
Kakitsubata has completed the boson jump.

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:13.550
Akatsuki-san? Akito-san? Yurika-san? Ryoko-san!

00:06:13.850 --> 00:06:15.530
Jun-san, change course to Mars.

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:19.060
I'm certain the Kakitsubata is headed for Mars.

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:23.280
Everything began and will end on Mars.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:23.860
Or else...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.990
Mars - Utopia Colony

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:47.750
Boson jump completed.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.490
Currently heading toward Utopia Colony Central Block.

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:52.510
So this is where they remember.

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:54.130
You know, Erina-kun,

00:06:54.130 --> 00:06:56.490
I don't think that breaking up those two is going to be possible.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.700
Are you insulting me?!

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:01.670
Boson jump has been successfully completed.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:02.940
All crew, return to normal operations mode.

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:04.390
What just happened?.

00:07:04.390 --> 00:07:05.470
All crew, return to normal operations mode.

00:07:05.470 --> 00:07:07.190
I guess I'm uncalled for.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:07.390
All crew, return to normal operations mode.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:08.250
Akito...

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:12.200
That was totally reckless!

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:16.910
If you had failed, all the crew of the Kakitsubata would be dead!

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:21.310
You don't have to worry. The crew of this ship was well aware and willing to take the chance.

00:07:21.310 --> 00:07:21.930
But...

00:07:21.930 --> 00:07:25.910
And more importantly, it's time for us to cheer!

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:28.840
The success of this experiment signifies a big step for humanity.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.870
You can scold me all you want later.

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:34.870
So what do you think, Doctor?

00:07:34.870 --> 00:07:37.900
Yes, I believe we unveiled the true nature of boson jumping.

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:39.890
But one thing bothers me.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:45.930
If boson jumping really does enable instantaneous movement between the Moon and Mars and such,

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:50.780
that refutes the absolute speed of light and Theory of Relativity.

00:07:51.270 --> 00:07:53.040
No one wants to consider that situation.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.360
Then what do you say it actually is?

00:07:54.820 --> 00:07:57.190
That's all I can say for the moment. The rest...

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.830
All depends on the outcome of the investigation of the ruins.

00:08:01.830 --> 00:08:02.370
Ruins?

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:04.140
Yes, the ruins.

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:16.590
It was all a coincidence.

00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:20.400
Nergal opened a mine on the Mars polar cap.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:23.190
A vast underground complex was uncovered in the process.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:28.380
It was comprised of the exact same molecular substance that Chulip Crystals are made of,

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:32.650
and there were some central parts of the ruin that are, to this day, still inactive.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:33.610
Question!

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:34.990
What is it?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.310
Why was this deemed to be so important?

00:08:37.310 --> 00:08:39.070
Was it some wonder weapon?

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.770
It appears that the ruins are merely a vast integrated system.

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:46.330
According to our research, whenever an object emerges from the Chulips,

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:50.010
or when the phenomenon that we refer to as a boson jump occurs,

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:52.700
we record increased activity coming from this system.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.080
In other words...

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.210
A boson jumping control system?

00:08:57.460 --> 00:08:58.840
But what is that?

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:01.200
If we could understand how the system works,

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:03.930
then we could dominate organic boson jumping.

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.970
If we can control the ruins before Earth and Jupiter can,

00:09:08.970 --> 00:09:10.680
then we would not only be able to stop the war,

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:16.360
but we would also hold the highest trump card as mankind begins its era of boson jump navigation.

00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:19.160
The company, the company... Climbing the ladder.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.680
What? Do you have a problem with that?

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:22.960
Oh, no. You're some great person, all right.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:29.050
This was your homeland, wasn't it?

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:36.570
The Utopia Colony? I'm a little jealous.

00:09:37.620 --> 00:09:39.220
For Akito-kun and the Captain...

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:40.710
the memorial land.

00:09:41.170 --> 00:09:44.830
What are you talking about?! I told you,

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.210
Yurika and I are not like that!

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.810
Yurika and I... Yurika and I are...

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:51.060
Damn it, what I'm trying to say is...

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.390
Make up your mind already.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:56.970
You're still a thickheaded bumbling fool, aren't you?

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:00.480
Really, bumbling fool.

00:10:00.890 --> 00:10:01.960
Us as well.

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:03.830
You two...

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.320
The Nadesico has entered Mars atmosphere.

00:10:07.320 --> 00:10:09.120
The Jovian Lizards have become active.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:09.750
It's about time.

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:12.090
Well, it's time to get ready!

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:14.440
Akito, are you all right?

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.120
Oh, sure, fine.

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.520
So, Chairman?

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:18.590
As we planned!

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.870
In other words, we will secure the ruins by working together, right?

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:24.720
Exactly! Now listen!

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.740
You're only going to end up sacrificing yourself if you jump to conclusions and act too gung-ho.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.950
So, why not? Why not fight for yourself?!

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:33.520
Let's do something really big for the finish!

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.670
It's time to pull the carpet from under Earth and Jupiter.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:44.580
Please understand, I plan to <i>be myself</i> during this fight.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.210
So, this will be a joint operation.

00:10:57.210 --> 00:10:58.460
Well, okay.

00:10:58.460 --> 00:11:00.940
It's not as if we have another choice at this point.

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:04.900
Ruri-chan, please give me the bearing and size of UEAF and Jovian forces in the vicinity.

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:05.300
Aye.

00:11:06.460 --> 00:11:10.650
The UEAF has amassed all its forces and departed from the Moon.

00:11:10.650 --> 00:11:12.250
They will arrive on Mars in about half a day.

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.060
Regarding the Jovian forces...

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:20.530
According to what Yukina-san has told us, this size is not an exaggeration.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:22.780
My, the Nadesico is like a speck.

00:11:23.110 --> 00:11:26.300
This gigantic convoy's aim is the colonization of Mars,

00:11:26.300 --> 00:11:29.240
and they also are about half a day's distance away.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:29.820
Which means...

00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:32.890
Mars will become a battlefield no later then half a day from now.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:33.710
Your decision, Captain?

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:36.130
We'll use the phase transition cannon!

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.050
All hands, battle stations! All hands, battle stations!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.110
The gravity might be weaker, but it's still the ground!

00:11:40.110 --> 00:11:42.370
All Aestivalis pilots, stand by in the cockpit.

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:44.470
Make sure everything's fully protected from dust and dirt!

00:11:45.320 --> 00:11:47.510
Yesterday, the Jovians. Today, Nergal.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:51.180
I'm not sure what we're fighting for any more.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:55.300
Ask me why I fight, I can only say that I fight because I am me.

00:11:55.590 --> 00:11:58.700
Only when you bet your life can you perceive the true odds.

00:12:00.200 --> 00:12:01.640
You're quite the poet today.

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.790
Hello, I'm Maki the Poetic Bard.

00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:07.610
Or was it Maki the Pathetic Broad?

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:13.700
I never could make sense out of Izumi-san's antics.

00:12:13.700 --> 00:12:14.340
Minato...

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.190
It's all right.

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:20.510
Jun-san and I will make up for Minato-san's absence.

00:12:21.960 --> 00:12:25.260
But not doing anything just makes things so much worse.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.780
I repeat, follow pattern Y. All hands, brace for impact.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.380
After we fire the phase transition cannon, change to pattern B.

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:33.130
I expect a smooth transition to normal battle stations.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:35.390
I leave phase transition cannon's formation to you.

00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:36.160
Expanding Y Unit.

00:12:36.160 --> 00:12:37.150
Change to pattern B.

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:39.570
Sarutahiko connected!

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:41.980
Phase transition engine's power to maximum.

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.870
Power output to maximum.

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:45.450
Damn it, Tenkawa!

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.290
What are you doing?! The fight's going to start at any moment!

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:49.480
Get in your Aestivalis!

00:12:49.770 --> 00:12:50.250
No.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.080
What?!

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:51.870
I don't want to!

00:12:51.990 --> 00:12:55.570
Why the hell are we fighting for Akatsuki, for the sake of Nergal?

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:56.780
For the benefit of a jerk like him?!

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:59.350
Because we have no other choice right now, jerk!

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:01.980
Because you say so? Damn!

00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.540
Stop whining like a baby!

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:04.260
What was that?!

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.990
Have some faith in her, Akito.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.200
Faith in the person who said she'd <i>be herself</i> through all this.

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:15.300
Ryoko-chan...

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:28.200
The ruins have been attacked?

00:13:29.030 --> 00:13:30.530
Immediate dispatch to the Yumemizuki and the Kannazuki!

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:31.150
Yes, Sir!

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:32.620
Jump ahead to Mars through organic leaping!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.060
We must not allow the city to fall into Earth's hands!

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:41.140
Enemy units defending the polar cap ruins have been decimated.

00:13:41.140 --> 00:13:43.640
Yes, that's more like it. I can work with that just fine.

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:45.720
My dear Captain, you did a wonderful job there!

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.000
You were very helpful too.

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.380
We could fire the phase transition cannon without worrying,

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:52.550
thanks to the Kakitsubata drawing the enemy's attention.

00:13:53.690 --> 00:13:56.490
Just remember, I want to be the first to enter the ruins.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:57.830
No playing tricks behind my back, okay?

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:00.940
Got that?

00:14:10.430 --> 00:14:12.870
The Kakitsubata has broken through the enemy perimeter.

00:14:12.870 --> 00:14:15.370
Continuing to move about the front as it destroys enemy forces.

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:17.700
Amazing agility.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:19.740
The Kakitsubata is really something.

00:14:19.740 --> 00:14:23.100
But it's going up against all the Jovian forces on Mars.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.380
So, Yurika...

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.750
Yes, continue firing the phase transition cannon.

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.600
Target, dead center on the polar cap ruins.

00:14:30.600 --> 00:14:31.260
Aye.

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.220
Wait just a minute!

00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:34.650
Is there something wrong with you, Misumaru Yurika?!

00:14:34.650 --> 00:14:36.350
There's nothing wrong with me.

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.570
There wouldn't be a war if it weren't for that thing.

00:14:38.820 --> 00:14:39.920
Fire the phase transition cannon.

00:14:39.920 --> 00:14:40.310
Wa... Wai...

00:14:40.310 --> 00:14:40.930
Aye.

00:14:40.940 --> 00:14:42.440
Hey! Wait!

00:14:47.640 --> 00:14:49.240
Detecting a field from within the ruins.

00:14:49.590 --> 00:14:51.400
Go ahead. Fire!

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:02.920
The ruins have cancelled the effect of the phase transition cannon.

00:15:02.920 --> 00:15:03.700
How'd that happen?

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:10.050
Oh, I knew it all along.

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:12.930
It was like hell getting to it in the first place,

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.970
going through thick ice and numerous distortion fields.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.690
That's not enough to do anything to it!

00:15:18.690 --> 00:15:19.760
You know you were worried.

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:21.270
Where are you going?

00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.690
To hop over to have a talk.

00:15:24.050 --> 00:15:25.350
Fire again!

00:15:28.030 --> 00:15:28.960
Oh, no...

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.030
What will we do, Yurika?

00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:31.590
Fire once more!

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:32.300
We cannot.

00:15:32.970 --> 00:15:34.490
There is not enough energy.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:38.330
The efficiency of the phase transition engine significantly decreases in atmosphere.

00:15:38.600 --> 00:15:40.160
Charging time twenty minutes.

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.010
Isn't there something you can do?

00:15:43.010 --> 00:15:43.890
Not a thing.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.590
The Kakitsubata is closing in fast.

00:15:47.200 --> 00:15:50.010
The Kakitsubata is launching Aestivalis units.

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:51.870
What will you do, Captain?

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:52.780
Yurika?

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:53.690
Captain?

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:55.920
Launch Aestivalis units!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:07.810
Please protect the Nadesico until we can fire the phase transition cannon.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:08.730
I'm counting on all of you!

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.660
I'd love to say no problem, but...

00:16:12.660 --> 00:16:14.190
Oh, boy. Here they come!

00:16:14.190 --> 00:16:15.780
Handsome himself showed up.

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:17.850
All right, ready to go?!

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:18.660
Sure!

00:16:22.030 --> 00:16:22.760
Akatsuki!

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:26.630
Shame on all of you. You should treasure cultural artifacts.

00:16:27.030 --> 00:16:31.480
Please, Akatsuki-san. We need to destroy the ruins and end the war.

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:33.710
So, is that your "being myself" talking?

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:36.930
You really are living out Gekiganger in every single way.

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:37.550
What was that?!

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:39.970
I've already left behind Gekiganger!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:40.470
Oh, really?

00:16:40.750 --> 00:16:42.390
Watching the Jovians, I understand now!

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.140
Understand what?

00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:45.980
That was the true nature of what I was so fond of!

00:16:45.980 --> 00:16:47.310
It's the enemy itself!

00:16:48.100 --> 00:16:50.730
Like I said, you're looking at it from only one side. Now listen.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:55.160
Just like every person has a different background, they also see justice as meaning different things.

00:16:55.730 --> 00:17:00.580
Incidentally, in the anime that I liked, both sides had just reasons for fighting.

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:03.110
Perhaps you should have watched a greater variety of anime as well.

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:05.380
Enough! Anime has nothing to do with this anymore!

00:17:05.380 --> 00:17:07.790
I just don't wasn't any more people suffering and crying!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:08.860
On either side!

00:17:14.990 --> 00:17:17.970
Listen here, Kakitsubata crew. Don't interfere.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:20.550
Ryoko-chan, I'll handle this, okay?

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:26.750
What do we do?

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.890
What else are we supposed to do but watch?

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:36.120
You'll end the war for the sake of the people and the world?

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.060
You certainly are distinguished people, aren't you!

00:17:41.230 --> 00:17:44.290
All you people think about is the sake of people and country? For the sake of the Earth?

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:46.950
All that just makes me want to puke!

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:49.800
He's got his rear!

00:17:49.800 --> 00:17:50.510
Akito?!

00:17:50.510 --> 00:17:51.840
Subaru-kun, cover him!

00:17:52.160 --> 00:17:54.050
We're busy as it is, damn it!

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:57.260
Weren't we supposed to just stand around and watch?

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.260
I'll let you in on a secret!

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:02.590
People who fight to be true to themselves can be really strong!

00:18:04.490 --> 00:18:06.150
Damn!

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:08.860
Visualize, see yourself jumping.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:13.230
What?! What's going on?

00:18:13.540 --> 00:18:14.900
He didn't use CCs?

00:18:15.750 --> 00:18:17.100
The power of the ruins?

00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:17.880
Correct.

00:18:23.390 --> 00:18:24.790
Get to Know the Nadesico!

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:27.580
Hello everyone. This is Inez Fressange.

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:31.790
This will be the last episode of everyone's favorite, Get to Know the Nadesico.

00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:35.500
Today, we will be drawing some deep insights into the nature of boson jumping.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:37.640
This will be a tough one, so pay close attention, everyone.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:38.650
Inez-san?

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:40.650
I've located the source of the transmission.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:41.430
14 km Underground
Source of Transmission
Surface of Polar Cap

00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:43.740
The deepest level of the ruins, about fourteen kilometers down

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:43.970
14 km Underground
Source of Transmission
Surface of Polar Cap

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:46.890
Inside the ruins? How did she get in there?

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.970
According to John Wheeler and Richard Feynman,

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:54.940
when we emit an electromagnetic wave, two waves are sent out,

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:56.860
the retarded wave and the advanced wave.

00:18:57.180 --> 00:19:00.100
The retarded wave travels along with time,

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:02.180
something like what we use to watch television with.

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:05.970
But the advanced wave travels opposite to time,

00:19:06.220 --> 00:19:07.750
and is emitted into the past.

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:11.040
Normally this advanced wave is absorbed by the retarded wave.

00:19:11.760 --> 00:19:15.960
But what if there was an unknown particle that's not influenced by the retarded wave?

00:19:16.490 --> 00:19:20.100
Matter converted into such a particle would go back in time!

00:19:20.100 --> 00:19:23.130
I have named such a particle, the retrospect.

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:28.360
If you think in these terms, then we can start to surmise that the boson jump,

00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:31.060
which we thought was spatial travel, was in fact time travel.

00:19:31.560 --> 00:19:33.880
If that assumption is correct,

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:40.740
then we might further assume that these ruins are in fact making all time lag adjustments.

00:19:41.420 --> 00:19:46.580
Movement in space-time is brought as the retrospect moves from present to past to present again.

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:51.310
And this is the massive computing engine that keeps track of it all, calculating without ever stopping.

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:55.220
If it didn't exist, boson jumps would probably be impossible.

00:19:55.780 --> 00:19:58.980
One reason that I came here is to test that hypothesis,

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:01.220
but I also have another reason.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.130
Akito-kun!

00:20:05.880 --> 00:20:07.870
Come here. We need to greet someone.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:16.630
Utopia Colony, Rainbow Elementary School,

00:20:17.430 --> 00:20:19.070
first grade, class five, number twelve.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:20.690
Favorite person,

00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:22.090
Mommy.

00:20:22.960 --> 00:20:23.960
Favorite food,

00:20:24.330 --> 00:20:25.060
spaghetti.

00:20:25.860 --> 00:20:26.980
Favorite book,

00:20:27.240 --> 00:20:28.230
Cinderella.

00:20:32.280 --> 00:20:35.280
It's all right. You don't need to cry.

00:20:37.970 --> 00:20:38.800
Welcome home.

00:21:47.060 --> 00:21:49.540
Ever since I was a child, I was taught that war was a bad thing.

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:52.330
When I hit a friend, something other than my fist hurt.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:55.660
But it also felt good to fight to protect a weaker friend.

00:21:55.990 --> 00:21:57.770
They said, there is no such thing as a righteous war.

00:21:57.770 --> 00:21:59.470
And it made me angry every time they talked of invasion.

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:02.340
We didn't want to turn right or left.

00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:04.870
It's just that none of the paths are for us.

00:22:05.140 --> 00:22:08.080
Next time! Martian Successor Nadesico, final episode!

00:22:08.080 --> 00:22:10.270
"For the Lady We Will Meet Someday"

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:12.190
Farewell, Nadesico.
